    <section ident="root_section">
      <item ident="gef0080b57475f8cefd54a716201180fa" title="Announcements">
        <itemmetadata>
          <qtimetadata>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>text_only_question</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>0.0</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry></fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>passage</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>true</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>assessment_question_identifierref</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>gf47b767d37e06559ff801f2d253307ba</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
          </qtimetadata>
        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="byui gs105"&gt;
&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #808080; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;div style="float: right; color: #ffffff; font-size: 26px; margin-left: 5px; padding: 5px; background-color: #808080;"&gt;Communication&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Announcements and Email&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are three main ways your instructor or the university can communicate with you throughout the semester:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Canvas Announcements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your instructor will be posting weekly announcements to give you an overview of the week. The announcement could include what topics are being covered each week, the due dates for assignments, and other relevant information. Checking announcements often will be one important factor in determining your success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Canvas Inbox&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instructors can also send important information to students through the Canvas inbox. Instructors use this method of communication when they need to contact one or more students about something. You can adjust your notification settings in Canvas and link your school email to your Canvas inbox. If you do this, all of the emails that come to your Canvas inbox will go directly to your school email account.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Canvas Feedback&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your instructor will leave feedback on any assignment not earning 100%. Many assignments build on each other so, applying the feedback received will help improve the score on future assignments. To find feedback on assignments, discussions, and quizzes, use the following steps:
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;strong&gt;Grades&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To the right of the activity (assignment, discussion, or quiz) for which you wish to see feedback.
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;img id="40240202" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/media/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20FeedbackIcon.png" alt="FeedbackIcon.png" loading="lazy"&gt; to view grader comments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;img id="40240200" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/media/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20RubricIcon.png" alt="RubricIcon.png" loading="lazy"&gt;to view rubrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Here are additional&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://byu-idaho.screenstepslive.com/s/16998/m/65436/l/1215037-how-do-i-find-assignment-feedback-copied?token=qFM5FwQ58hAh15jjX9U5WF2v0MXTI2-m" target="_blank"&gt;tutorials&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </presentation>
      </item>
