      <item ident="g6a6ab6567e6f44c58df66db97e8dc99d" title="Canvas Notification">
        <itemmetadata>
          <qtimetadata>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>true_false_question</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>296,479</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>assessment_question_identifierref</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>g6cec9a549edb067496d6fe32f1651131</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
          </qtimetadata>
        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://community.canvaslms.com/t5/Student-Guide/How-do-I-add-contact-methods-to-receive-Canvas-notifications-as/ta-p/516" target="_blank"&gt;Add your contact methods in Canvas&lt;/a&gt; so you can receive notifications, in your preferred delivery (text or email).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://community.instructure.com/en/kb/articles/662894-how-do-i-manage-my-canvas-notification-settings?utm_source=community-search&amp;amp;utm_medium=organic-search&amp;amp;utm_term=Set+your+notification+preferences+in+Canvas" target="_blank"&gt;Set your notification preferences in Canvas&lt;/a&gt; so you can be updated whenever there is a new announcement, comment or grade on your assignment, discussion update, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Image Explanation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The green bell means you will be notified immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The green page means you will be notified at the end of the day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The green calendar means you will be notified at the end of the week.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The white bell means you do not want this notification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img id="60347678" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/media/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20Notifications.JPG" alt="Course Notifications screenshot showing a green calendar icon for Due dates and Grading Polices and showing a green bell icon for announcements." width="350" height="325" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;T/F: I can set notifications individually for each course.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
          <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
            <render_choice>
              <response_label ident="296">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">True</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
              <response_label ident="479">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">False</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
            </render_choice>
          </response_lid>
        </presentation>
        <resprocessing>
          <outcomes>
            <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
          </outcomes>
          <respcondition continue="No">
            <conditionvar>
              <varequal respident="response1">296</varequal>
            </conditionvar>
            <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
          </respcondition>
        </resprocessing>
      </item>
      <item ident="g3086b84931f52252cc3fe7880ba746b6" title="Syllabus - Late Work">
        <itemmetadata>
          <qtimetadata>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>multiple_answers_question</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>6188,4476,9899,9986</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>assessment_question_identifierref</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>gf47b767d37e06559ff801f2d253307ba</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
          </qtimetadata>
        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What two options below did the syllabus tell you about late work?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
          <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Multiple">
            <render_choice>
              <response_label ident="6188">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">As a sign of professionalism and respect, work should be submitted on time.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
              <response_label ident="4476">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">Late work is never accepted.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
              <response_label ident="9899">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">Late work will receive a 0, though work may still be submitted for points.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
              <response_label ident="9986">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">Late work is not graded.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
            </render_choice>
          </response_lid>
        </presentation>
        <resprocessing>
          <outcomes>
            <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
          </outcomes>
          <respcondition continue="No">
            <conditionvar>
              <and>
                <varequal respident="response1">6188</varequal>
                <not>
                  <varequal respident="response1">4476</varequal>
                </not>
                <varequal respident="response1">9899</varequal>
                <not>
                  <varequal respident="response1">9986</varequal>
                </not>
              </and>
            </conditionvar>
            <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
          </respcondition>
        </resprocessing>
      </item>
      <item ident="gb8fda6482d3049bf52005d89549b79ea" title="Question">
        <itemmetadata>
          <qtimetadata>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>3485,3389,1608</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>assessment_question_identifierref</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>gf47b767d37e06559ff801f2d253307ba</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
          </qtimetadata>
        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #808080; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Academic Honesty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students taking courses through BYU-Idaho are expected to follow BYU-Idaho's &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy.&lt;/a&gt; This includes avoiding plagiarism, fabrication or falsification, cheating, academic misconduct, and unauthorized uploading or sharing. BYU-Idaho takes academic honesty seriously and violations of the Academic Honesty Policy may result in consequences up to and including suspension or expulsion from the university.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cody and Angie are both in the same course but in different sections. Cody needed to take Quiz 1, a timed open-note, open-book, but not an open-person test. Since he had been busy at his job and dating Angie, he did not finish reading the assigned chapters. He had planned on organizing his material before the test but needed to help his friend who was sick. Panicked, he called Angie who had already taken the quiz, and asked her what questions were on the quiz.&amp;nbsp; Was this academically honest?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
          <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
            <render_choice>
              <response_label ident="3485">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes, it is academically honest. Cody made an attempt to study but was too busy to finish the study guides.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
              <response_label ident="3389">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes. It is academically honest. It is important for students to help one another through difficult times.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
              <response_label ident="1608">
                <material>
                  <mattext texttype="text/plain">No. It is not academically honest. Asking someone who has taken the test what was on it is academically dishonest.</mattext>
                </material>
              </response_label>
            </render_choice>
          </response_lid>
        </presentation>
        <resprocessing>
          <outcomes>
            <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
          </outcomes>
          <respcondition continue="No">
            <conditionvar>
              <varequal respident="response1">1608</varequal>
            </conditionvar>
            <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
          </respcondition>
        </resprocessing>
      </item>
